DEFINITION MODULE PortIO;

(* Z80 port input and output for FTL Modula-2.

   FTL has no port I/O in the language: SYSTEM exports no IN or OUT, and the
   SYSTEM.OUT this library used under Turbo Modula-2 does not exist here.  Port
   access is a library module over two assembly entries.

   SIGNATURE-COMPATIBLE WITH THE STOCK FTL PortIO, deliberately.  Dave Moore
   ships PORTIO.DEF and PORTIO.ASM in DEFFILES.LQR and ASMFILES.LQR, but alone
   among his assembly modules it has no prebuilt PORTIO.REL or PORTIO.SYM in
   SYMFILES.LQR or MODULA2.LQR -- CHAIN, CPM, CPMBIOS, EXCHANGE, FASTMOVE and
   INTLOGIC all do.  An FTL installation that has had PortIO compiled into its
   libraries can therefore drop this module and Sound will link unchanged; the
   copy of the distribution carried in Software/disk1/5 has not, which is why
   this is built from source here and the project build stays self-contained.

   Deliberately narrower than the stock module, which also exports
   DisableInterrupts, EnableInterrupts and SetMode2Base.  None of those belong
   on this machine: SetMode2Base sets the I register and the BIOS owns IM2 --
   see the CTCLow bridge -- and bare DI/EI would cut across the BIOS interrupt
   contracts.  Importing only In and Out keeps that true either way.

   Val is WORD to match the stock interface.  Sound passes CARDINAL and FTL
   accepts it; this was checked by building Sound against both signatures.

   The procedure order below is load-bearing: the LABEL exports in PORTIO.ASM
   must follow it. *)

FROM SYSTEM IMPORT WORD;

PROCEDURE In(PortAddress : CARDINAL) : WORD;
PROCEDURE Out(PortAddress : CARDINAL; Val : WORD);

END PortIO.
